{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Fred2005.FormalGroups","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Fred2005.FormalGroups","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic"],"declarations":47,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.unit_root_iff_integrable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.unit_root_iff_integrable","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L299-L318","doc":"The unit-root condition on an F-crystal is equivalent to\nintegrability of the associated skewed-Poisson structure:\n`π_<` integrates iff the F-crystal is unit-root.\n\nForward direction: the integration theorem produces `G` from `π`.\nBackward direction: the identity endomorphism witnesses unit-root.\n\nReference: [fred2005, Corollary 5.3]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:unit-root-iff-integrable","label":"thm:unit-root-iff-integrable","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/unit-root-iff-integrable.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.frobenius_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.frobenius_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L297-L297","doc":"The Frobenius is surjective (unit-root condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.frobenius_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.frobenius_injective","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L295-L295","doc":"The Frobenius is injective (unit-root condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.frobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.frobenius","kind":"def","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L293-L293","doc":"The Frobenius endomorphism on the coordinate ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L291-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.UnitRootFCrystal","kind":"structure","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L286-L297","doc":"**Unit-root F-crystal**: an F-crystal is unit-root when the\nFrobenius acts invertibly on the coordinate ring — no nilpotent\npart in the Dieudonné–Manin decomposition.\n\nReference: [hazewinkel1978, Ch. V], [zink2002, §2]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:unit-root-f-crystal","label":"def:unit-root-f-crystal","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/unit-root-f-crystal.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.witt_vector_lift_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.witt_vector_lift_exists","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L273-L282","doc":"The Witt vector lift exists for any commutative formal group\nequipped with a skewed-Poisson structure.\n\nReference: [fred2005, Main Theorem + §5]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:witt-vector-lift-exists","label":"thm:witt-vector-lift-exists","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/witt-vector-lift-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.WittVectorLift.reduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.WittVectorLift.reduces","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L271-L271","doc":"Reduction: `G mod p ≅ H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.WittVectorLift.lifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.WittVectorLift.lifted","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L269-L269","doc":"The lifted non-commutative formal group `G / ℤ_p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.WittVectorLift.poisson","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.WittVectorLift.poisson","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L267-L267","doc":"The skewed-Poisson structure driving the deformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.WittVectorLift.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.WittVectorLift.base","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L265-L265","doc":"The commutative formal group `H / 𝔽_p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.WittVectorLift.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.WittVectorLift.mk","kind":"ctor","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L263-L263","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.WittVectorLift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.WittVectorLift","kind":"structure","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L257-L271","doc":"**Witt vector lift**: given a commutative formal group `H / 𝔽_p`\nwith skewed-Poisson structure, the Witt vector functor `W` produces\na formal group `Ĝ / ℤ_p` whose generic fibre is a non-commutative\nformal group over `ℚ_p`.\n\nReference: [fred2005, §5], [hazewinkel1978, Ch. V]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:witt-vector-lift","label":"def:witt-vector-lift","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/witt-vector-lift.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.strong_multiplicativity_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.strong_multiplicativity_holds","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L228-L253","doc":"**Strong multiplicativity** of a non-commutative formal group: the\ncomultiplication is an algebra homomorphism, `Δ(xy) = Δ(x)·Δ(y)` componentwise.\n\nNOTE (honest disposition, 2026-07-18; AUTHOR TO VERIFY): this is the\n**defining `comul_hom` axiom** of `NoncommutativeFormalGroup`, restated as a\nnamed accessor. The previous version carried unused `(gsb) (_hgsb)` hypotheses\nand a docstring claiming it *proved* [fred2005, Thm 4.12] (\"preserved under the\nGS deformation at every filtration degree\") — but the proof was `:= G.comul_hom`,\na projection of `G`'s own axiom, using neither hypothesis. The misleading\nhypotheses and framing are removed: this lemma asserts only that a group *which\nis* a `NoncommutativeFormalGroup` satisfies strong multiplicativity **by\ndefinition**. The substantive dissertation result — that the *constructed*\n`Dist(G)` (from `skew_poisson_integrates`) actually satisfies it, preserved at\nevery filtration degree — is [fred2005, Thm 4.12], cited there, and is NOT a\nconsequence of this accessor. (Expressing \"at every filtration degree\" needs a\nfiltered-deformation structure the current model does not carry — a genuine\nfollow-up for a fuller fred2005 formalization.)\n\nReference: [fred2005, Theorem 4.12]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:strong-multiplicativity","label":"thm:strong-multiplicativity","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/strong-multiplicativity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.grobner_shirshov_basis_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.grobner_shirshov_basis_exists","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L199-L224","doc":"The Gröbner–Shirshov basis for `Dist(G)` exists and yields\na flat deformation of `Dist(H)`.\n\nNOTE (honest disposition, 2026-07-18; AUTHOR TO VERIFY): the previous proof\ndischarged `∃ gsb, gsb.formalGroup = G` with the **trivial identity\nreduction** (`reduce = embed = id`), which its own docstring admitted \"the\nnon-trivial content is that the q-Serre relations form a Gröbner–Shirshov\nsystem\" — i.e. the witness did not capture the theorem. The conclusion is now\nstrengthened to require a **genuinely reductive** basis: distinct elements\nshare a normal form (`∃ a b, a ≠ b ∧ reduce a = reduce b`), which the identity\nreduction does NOT satisfy, encoding that `Dist(G)` carries real (q-Serre)\nrelations. Constructing the divided-power / Lusztig canonical basis and\nverifying the composition lemma (confluence) is [fred2005, Prop. 3.8 &\nThm 3.15]; it is stated here with `sorry`, cited, not re-derived.\n\nReference: [fred2005, Proposition 3.8 and Theorem 3.15]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","label":"thm:grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.composition_lemma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.composition_lemma","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L196-L196","doc":"The composition lemma (confluence): reduction is a retraction,\ni.e. `reduce ∘ embed ∘ reduce = reduce`.  This ensures all\nS-polynomials of leading monomials reduce to zero.\n[fred2005, Proposition 3.8] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.embed","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L191-L191","doc":"An embedding from normal forms back to `Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.reduce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.reduce","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L189-L189","doc":"A reduction map taking elements of `Dist(G)` to normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.spans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.spans","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L187-L187","doc":"The normal forms span `Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.normalForms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.normalForms","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L185-L185","doc":"The set of normal-form monomials (abstract type). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.formalGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.formalGroup","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L183-L183","doc":"The formal group whose distribution algebra is being presented. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L181-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.GrobnerShirshovBasis","kind":"structure","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L175-L197","doc":"**Gröbner–Shirshov basis** for the relations of `Dist(G)`.\nThe composition lemma guarantees that the leading monomials of the\n`q`-Serre relations provide non-overlapping obstructions, yielding\na normal-form basis coinciding with the Lusztig divided-power basis.\n\nReference: [fred2005, §3]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:grobner-shirshov-basis","label":"def:grobner-shirshov-basis","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/grobner-shirshov-basis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.reduction_mod_p_commutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.reduction_mod_p_commutative","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L159-L171","doc":"**Reduction modulo p**: the non-commutative formal group `G / ℤ_p`\nreduces to the commutative formal group `H / 𝔽_p` modulo `p`.\nConcretely, the base formal group law is commutative.\n\nReference: [fred2005, Main Theorem, item (1)]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:reduction-mod-p","label":"thm:reduction-mod-p","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/reduction-mod-p.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.skew_poisson_integrates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.skew_poisson_integrates","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L125-L157","doc":"**Integration theorem** ([fred2005, Main Theorem]):\nA skewed-Poisson structure on a commutative formal group `H / 𝔽_p`\nintegrates to a non-commutative formal group `G / ℤ_p`.\n\nThe construction uses `H.coordRing` as the distribution algebra,\nthe formal group law deformed by the bracket as multiplication,\nand the diagonal as comultiplication (group-like elements).\n\nReference: [fred2005, Main Theorem].\n\nNOTE (honest disposition, 2026-07-18; AUTHOR TO VERIFY): the witness below is a\n*faithful* construction — the distribution algebra is `H.coordRing`, the\nmultiplication is the **bracket-deformed product** `mul x y = F(x, π_<(x,y))`,\nand the comultiplication is the group-like diagonal (per the construction note\nabove). What this existence statement does NOT capture — and must not be read as\nproving — is the substantive dissertation content: that this data assembles into\na genuine non-commutative formal group whose *full* `Dist(G)` satisfies strong\nmultiplicativity at every filtration degree (the diagonal comultiplication makes\n`comul_hom` hold trivially, so the deep Frobenius-preservation claim is\nelsewhere). That is [fred2005, Main Theorem], cited, not re-derived here.\n(A statement pinning `G.mul` to the deformed product cannot be written directly:\n`G.distAlgebra` is existentially abstract, so `G.mul` and the `H.coordRing`\nfunction are not comparable without a carrier identification.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:skew-poisson-integrates","label":"thm:skew-poisson-integrates","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/skew-poisson-integrates.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.comul_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.comul_hom","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L119-L119","doc":"**Strong multiplicativity**: the comultiplication is an algebra\nhomomorphism, i.e. `Δ(xy) = Δ(x) · Δ(y)` component-wise.\nThis is the key condition from [fred2005, Theorem 4.12]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.unit","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L115-L115","doc":"The identity element of `Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.comul","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The comultiplication on `Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.mul","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The multiplication on `Dist(G)` (generally non-commutative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.distAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.distAlgebra","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Carrier type of `Dist(G)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.base","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L107-L107","doc":"The commutative base group `H / 𝔽_p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup","kind":"structure","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L100-L121","doc":"**Non-commutative formal group**: the output of the integration\ntheorem.  This is the formal group `G` over `ℤ_p` whose distribution\nalgebra is the Gröbner–Shirshov deformation of `Dist(H)`.\n\nReference: [fred2005, Main Theorem]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:non-commutative-formal-group","label":"def:non-commutative-formal-group","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/non-commutative-formal-group.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.jacobi_truncated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.jacobi_truncated","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The `p`-truncated Jacobi condition:\n`π_<(f, π_<(g, h)) + π_<(g, π_<(h, f)) + π_<(h, π_<(f, g)) = 0`\nmodulo `p`-th powers.\n[fred2005, §2, Definition 2.3] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Graded anti-symmetry: `π_<(f, g) = −π_<(g, f)`.\n[fred2005, §2, Definition 2.3] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.neg","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Negation on the coordinate ring (needed for anti-symmetry). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.bracket","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The biderivation `π_<` (abstract map on coordinate rings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.SkewedPoissonStructure","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L70-L96","doc":"**Skewed-Poisson structure** on a commutative formal group `H`.\nA biderivation `π_< : 𝒪(H) ⊗ 𝒪(H) → 𝒪(H)` satisfying graded\nanti-symmetry and a `p`-truncated Jacobi condition.\n\nThis is the infinitesimal datum that encodes the non-commutativity\nto be \"integrated\" into a non-commutative formal group.\n\nReference: [fred2005, §2, Definition 2.3]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:skewed-poisson-structure","label":"def:skewed-poisson-structure","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/skewed-poisson-structure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.zero","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The zero element of the coordinate ring.\nEvery formal group law satisfies `F(X, 0) = X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.commutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.commutative","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The formal group law is commutative: `F(X,Y) = F(Y,X)`.\n[hazewinkel1978, Ch. I] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.formalGroupLaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.formalGroupLaw","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The formal group law `F : 𝒪(H) → 𝒪(H) → 𝒪(H)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.coordRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.coordRing","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Carrier type of the coordinate ring `𝒪(H)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.p_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.p_prime","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L56-L56","doc":"`p` is prime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.p","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The prime characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"Fred2005.CommutativeFormalGroup","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/fred2005-formal-groups/lean/Fred2005/FormalGroups.lean#L48-L66","doc":"**Commutative formal group** over a field `k` of characteristic `p`.\nThis is the \"base\" object `H` in the dissertation's integration theorem.\n\nReference: [hazewinkel1978, Ch. I]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:commutative-formal-group","label":"def:commutative-formal-group","md":"fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/commutative-formal-group.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}